# Target C — terminal FREE metric currency forces a train/face floor

**Date:** 2026-09-18
**Status:** proof-only synthesis; theorem-state authority unchanged
**Scope:** full-core Type-II survivor sequences carrying a non-anchored all-inactive FREE reflection module; terminal consequences additionally assume `pi D-q=o(D)`
**Depends on:** the FREE boundary-crossing metric-routing theorem, the exact loaded-hull identity `b+Q=2(q-k)`, and the audited-working all-defect phase/train gap
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_free_terminal_train_face_bridge_2026_09_18.py`
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The preceding FREE metric-routing theorem ends with a recipient inequality in the
actual outer-walk detour

\[
\lambda_D:=b-\operatorname{per}(F),
\]

the exterior isolate population `Z_ext`, and the force-hull side-length surplus

\[
H_D:=\operatorname{per}(F)-q.
\]

This note eliminates `lambda_D` exactly by inserting the canonical loaded-hull face
identity.  On the terminal face it then inserts the independent all-defect train/face
gap.  The result is a direct lower bound on the high-`t` variable

\[
t_D:={q-k\over D},\qquad k=d_H+s_Z,
\]

with an explicit linear tradeoff against `Z_ext/D`.

The main asymptotic consequence is

\[
\boxed{
\liminf\left({q-k\over D}+{2\over5}{Z_{\rm ext}\over D}\right)
\ge
{\pi\over2}+{1\over5}
+{2\over5}\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{2\sqrt3}}
=2.151721449540479\ldots
}
\tag{FT.1}
\]

on every terminal FREE survivor sequence in the stated scope.  In particular,

\[
Z_{\rm ext}=o(D)
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\boxed{
\liminf {q-k\over D}\ge2.151721449540479\ldots .
}
\tag{FT.2}
\]

Thus the small-external terminal FREE branch lies strictly beyond the entire
`t<=1.8687` high-`t` rectangle studied by the September 17 support-normal-form
pipeline.  Conversely, a terminal FREE survivor with `t<=1.8687+o(1)` must satisfy

\[
\boxed{
Z_{\rm ext}\ge(0.707553623851198\ldots-o(1))D.
}
\tag{FT.3}
\]

This is a branch reduction, not a C-II closure.  A large exterior population is still
allowed, and the proof-only all-defect input is not promoted here.

---

## 1. Exact finite elimination of the outer-walk detour

Use the notation of the FREE boundary-crossing metric-routing theorem.  Its finite
inequality is

\[
\lambda_D+Z_{\rm ext}+(C_{H,D}+1)H_D
\ge
S_D+1-\sigma_D-C_{\Delta,D}\Delta_D,
\tag{FT.4}
\]

where:

- `S_D` is the original monotone parent-chain support span;
- `sigma_D` is its total edge-length slack, bounded by `h_*+D^{-1/3}`;
- `Delta_D` is the bounded crossing-side clearing correction;
- `C_{H,D},C_{Delta,D}` stay bounded as `D->infinity`.

The use of `sigma_D` here avoids overloading the high-`t` variable `t_D`.

Canonical loaded-hull algebra gives the exact finite identity

\[
\boxed{b+Q=2(q-k).}
\tag{FT.5}
\]

Since

\[
\operatorname{per}(F)=q+H_D,
\]

we have, exactly,

\[
\begin{aligned}
\lambda_D
&=b-\operatorname{per}(F)\\
&=2(q-k)-Q-q-H_D.
\end{aligned}
\tag{FT.6}
\]

Substitute (FT.6) into (FT.4).  The extra `+H_D` in the coefficient of (FT.4)
cancels the `-H_D` inside `lambda_D`.  Therefore

\[
\boxed{
2(q-k)+Z_{\rm ext}+C_{H,D}H_D
\ge
q+Q+S_D+1-\sigma_D-C_{\Delta,D}\Delta_D.
}
\tag{FT.7}
\]

This is the useful finite bridge.  It converts the FREE corridor directly into the
same `q-k` and `Q` currencies used by the full-core train/face ledger, with no estimate
on `b` beyond the exact identity (FT.5).

---

## 2. Terminal normalization

Assume now

\[
\pi D-q=o(D).
\tag{FT.8}
\]

Because `q<=per(F)<=pi D`, (FT.8) also gives

\[
H_D=\operatorname{per}(F)-q=o(D).
\tag{FT.9}
\]

The FREE parent-chain theorem gives

\[
{S_D\over D}\to{1\over2},
\tag{FT.10}
\]

while `sigma_D=O(1)`, `Delta_D=O(1)`, and both clearing coefficients remain bounded.
Write the normalized finite quantities

\[
t_D={q-k\over D},
\qquad
z_D={Z_{\rm ext}\over D},
\qquad
\phi_D={Q\over D}.
\]

Dividing (FT.7) by `D` and using (FT.8)--(FT.10) gives directly

\[
\boxed{
2t_D+z_D\ge\pi+\phi_D+{1\over2}-o(1).
}
\tag{FT.11}
\]

In particular,

\[
2t_D+z_D\ge\pi+{1\over2}-o(1).
\tag{FT.12}
\]

If `z_D=o(1)`, (FT.12) alone gives
`t_D>=1.82079632679...-o(1)`; the next section raises that coefficient to
`2.15172...`.

---

## 3. Insert the all-defect phase/train gap

Let `f` be the number of bounded nonquadrilateral contact faces.  The audited-working
all-defect phase/train theorem gives, for every Type-II full-core survivor,

\[
2f-k\ge(\gamma-o(1))D,
\tag{FT.13}
\]

where

\[
\Delta_2={\pi\over2\sqrt3},
\qquad
\gamma=2\sqrt{\Delta_2}-{\pi\over2}
=0.333829286933018\ldots .
\tag{FT.14}
\]

Every bounded nonquadrilateral face has degree at least five.  Hence, for

\[
Q=\sum_P(\deg P-4),
\]

one has the exact discrete inequality

\[
\boxed{Q\ge f.}
\tag{FT.15}
\]

On the terminal branch,

\[
{k\over D}
={q\over D}-t_D
=\pi-t_D+o(1).
\tag{FT.16}
\]

Equations (FT.13)--(FT.16) therefore imply the finite asymptotic lower bound

\[
\boxed{
\phi_D\ge {\pi-t_D+\gamma\over2}-o(1).
}
\tag{FT.17}
\]

Insert (FT.17) into (FT.11):

\[
2t_D+z_D
\ge
\pi+{1\over2}+{\pi-t_D+\gamma\over2}-o(1).
\]

Thus

\[
\boxed{5t_D+2z_D\ge3\pi+1+\gamma-o(1).}
\tag{FT.18}
\]

Using (FT.14),

\[
\boxed{
t_D+{2\over5}z_D
\ge
{\pi\over2}+{1\over5}
+{2\over5}\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{2\sqrt3}}
-o(1).
}
\tag{FT.19}
\]

Taking `liminf` proves (FT.1), and `z_D=o(1)` proves (FT.2).

---

## 4. Quantitative external-population price below the new floor

Rearranging (FT.18) gives

\[
\boxed{
z_D\ge
{3\pi+1+\gamma-5t_D\over2}-o(1).
}
\tag{FT.20}
\]

For a few reference values:

\[
\begin{array}{c|c}
T & t\le T\ \Longrightarrow\ \liminf Z_{\rm ext}/D\\ \hline
1.8440 & 0.769303623851198\ldots\\
1.8600 & 0.729303623851198\ldots\\
1.8687 & 0.707553623851198\ldots\\
2.0000 & 0.379303623851198\ldots
\end{array}
\tag{FT.21}
\]

The `1.8687` row proves (FT.3).  Therefore a terminal FREE survivor cannot live in the
entire September-17 bounded high-`t` support-normal-form window unless a positive
linear exterior-isolate population survives simultaneously.

At the formal `z=0` equality point of the scalar relaxation,

\[
t=2.151721449540479\ldots,
\qquad
{k\over D}=\pi-t=0.989871204049314\ldots,
\]

and (FT.17) requires

\[
{Q\over D}\ge {f\over D}\ge0.661850245491166\ldots .
\tag{FT.22}
\]

At this formal equality point all scalar inequalities are tight, so

\[
{\lambda_D\over D}
=2t-\pi-{Q\over D}
={1\over2}.
\]

More generally, when `z_D=o(1)` the original terminal FREE recipient law gives
`lambda_D/D>=1/2-o(1)` directly, while (FT.17) supplies the independent lower bound on
`Q/D`.  Their compatibility is exactly what produces (FT.2).  The scalar endpoint
therefore carries both a half-diameter of actual outer-walk detour and a linear
exceptional-face population.

---

## 5. Scope audit and next target

The argument uses only quantities from the same full-core source:

1. (FT.7) is a finite algebraic composition of the proved FREE metric-routing
   inequality with the exact canonical identity `b+Q=2(q-k)`.
2. The terminal passage uses `pi D-q=o(D)`, which itself implies `H_D=o(D)` because
   `q<=per(F)<=pi D`.
3. The strengthening from `1.82079...` to `2.15172...` uses the separate
   audited-working all-defect phase/train theorem.  This note does not promote that
   theorem or hide its proof-only status.
4. No assumption `Z_ext=o(D)` is needed for the tradeoff (FT.19); that assumption is
   used only for the clean floor (FT.2).
5. Nothing here bounds `Z_ext/D` from above.  Hence the result does not close the FREE
   branch and does not close C-II.

The remaining terminal FREE branch is now split sharply:

```text
large exterior branch:
    Z_ext = Omega(D), with the exact price (FT.20),

or small-exterior branch:
    (q-k)/D >= 2.15172144954...,
    outside the entire t<=1.8687 high-t rectangle,
    with linear Q/f and at least half a diameter of metric outer-walk detour.
```

The next useful step is therefore not another refinement inside the old `t<=1.8687`
rectangle.  It is either:

- an upper bound on `Z_ext/D` in the terminal full-core geometry strong enough to feed
  (FT.19); or
- a new large-`t` argument beginning at `t>=2.15172...` and using the simultaneous
  `lambda_D/D>=1/2-o(1)` and linear defect-face population.

**Disposition:** exact finite FREE-to-train/face bridge proved; terminal combination
with the audited-working all-defect phase gap yields the new
`t+(2/5)Z_ext/D >= 2.15172144954...` tradeoff.  The authoritative theorem-state ledger
is unchanged; C-II remains open.
